  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper reports three gate-based quantum simulation experiments on Cirq: VQE for H2, LiH, and H2O with energies -1.132, -7.865, and -74.953 Hartree versus FCI values -1.137, -7.882, and -75.012; VQE for 1D Fermi-Hubbard at N=2,4 and U/t=1.0,4.0 with energies -2.231, -1.512, -4.683, and -3.187 versus exact values -2.236, -1.528, -4.728, and -3.256; and QAE-style European option pricing with relative errors of 3.2%, 1.5%, 0.7%, and 0.3% at target precisions 4, 6, 8, and 10 bits. The paper uses only classical simulation and provides theoretical scaling claims for QAE (O(1/ε) vs O(1/ε^2)) but no demonstrated practical quantum advantage.",
